From: "lich.wang" <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] input: nt36532: parent the input devices to the SPI device

The vendor driver allocates the touchscreen and pen input devices
without a parent, so they appear under /sys/devices/virtual/input.
User space then sees them as virtual devices: InputPlumber skips every
device under /devices/virtual, and udev cannot give them an ID_PATH.
Parent both to the SPI device, as input drivers normally do.

Effects in user space: gamescope associates real (non-virtual) touch
devices with the panel, so it now maps the TB710FU touchscreen to the
internal display (orientation normal on this board). InputPlumber now
considers both devices, but no InputPlumber profile matches the TB710FU,
so nothing manages or grabs them; this is a prerequisite for one.
libinput device groups, hwdb matches and the desktop touchscreen setup
match on phys, modalias or name and do not change.

Only the TB710FU binds this driver (novatek,nt36532-ts-spi).

Tested on TB710FU (unified kernel 7.2.6, InputPlumber 0.81.0): both
devices are under .../a90000.spi/spi_master/spi0/spi0.0/input/, udev
sets ID_PATH=platform-a90000.spi-cs-0, the touchscreen and the pen
register, /proc/support_pen stays 1, and InputPlumber lists them as
source devices without creating a CompositeDevice. In Game Mode finger
touch lands where it should (checked by hand after switching from the
desktop and back), and the pen still works as a tablet on the desktop.
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c
@@ -2928,6 +2928,7 @@
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto err_input_dev_alloc_failed;
 	}
+	ts->input_dev->dev.parent = &client->dev;
 
 	ts->max_touch_num = TOUCH_MAX_FINGER_NUM;
 
@@ -3007,6 +3008,7 @@
 			ret = -ENOMEM;
 			goto err_pen_input_dev_alloc_failed;
 		}
+		ts->pen_input_dev->dev.parent = &client->dev;
 		nvt_pen_input_config();
 		//---register pen input device---
 		ret = input_register_device(ts->pen_input_dev);
